Integration Workflow:
Frontend (HTML, CSS, JavaScript):

Users interact with the interface (search movies, submit reviews, etc.).
Uses AJAX or Fetch API to send HTTP requests to the Node.js + Express.js backend.
Backend (Node.js + Express.js):

MongoDB for database

Stores user data, movie details, and reviews.
Backend uses MySQL drivers (like mysql2 or sequelize) to perform CRUD operations.
ML Model (TensorFlow):
You have two integration options:

Flask API:
Deploy the TensorFlow model in a separate Flask server.
Node.js makes HTTP requests to the Flask API to send user reviews and get sentiment predictions.
TensorFlow.js (Direct Integration):
If you want the ML model to run directly in the browser or Node.js without a separate server.
Good for simpler models but less efficient for complex ones.
🔗 Example Flow:
User submits a review → Frontend sends it to → Node.js Backend.
Backend sends review to → TensorFlow model → gets sentiment.
Backend stores review & sentiment in → MySQL Database.
Frontend fetches updated data → displays to user.